<title>GERMANY: ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S WORLD CUP DOWNHILL TRAINING TIMES.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S WORLD CUP DOWNHILL TRAINING TIMES.</headline>
<dateline>GARMISCH-PARTENKIRCHEN, Germany 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading</p>
<p>times in Thursday's training for the ninth men's World Cup</p>
<p>downhill of the Alpine skiing season at the weekend: </p>
<p>  1. Luc Alphand (France)	  one minute 57.88 seconds</p>
<p>  2. Kristian Ghedina (Italy)    1:58.36</p>
<p>  3. Pietro Vitalini (Italy)     1:58.44</p>
<p>  4. Franco Cavegn (Switzerland) 1:59.49</p>
<p>  5. Jean-Luc Cretier (France)   1:59.53</p>
<p>  6. Fritz Strobl (Austria)	1:59.90</p>
<p>  7. Urs Lehmann (Switzerland)   2.00.08</p>
<p>  8. Ed Podivinsky (Canada)	2:00.10</p>
<p>  9. Cary Mullen (Canada)	  2:00.27</p>
<p> 10. Erik Seletto (Italy)	  2:00.30</p>
</text>
